  "reference_carrier_known_debt": {
    "TM2.b": {
      "count": 3,
      "why": "Minimum TopMetal2 space or notch, 2 um. Was 40 before the exporter's notch heal; the 37 it closed were notches inside one piece of copper, mostly where a trace takes its first bend while still inside a round Cu-pillar pad and so leaves the pad almost tangentially. The 3 that remain all sit on the left edge of a 100 x 100 um wire-bond pad, which the heal stays out of on purpose: Pad.fR measures its 7 um exit band from the edge where the trace crosses the pad marker, so widening the trace there lengthens that edge and enlarges the band that has to stay covered. Healing them was measured and it moved Pad.fR_TM2 from 27 markers to 30 and its uncovered area from 450 to 466 um2, i.e. it traded a notch for a bigger exit violation. Closing these 3 is the same layout fix as Pad.fR_TM2: leave the bond pad orthogonally for 7 um before turning."
    },
    "Pad.fR_TM2": {
      "count": 27,
      "why": "Recommended, not mandatory (IHP marks recommendations with the R suffix): minimum TopMetal2 exit length of 7 um from a pad. Each marker is the corner of the 7 um exit band left uncovered because the trace leaves the bond pad diagonally. Appeared when the bond pads gained their dfpad and passivation opening, which is what makes them pads to the deck at all; before that the same pads were 35 hard Slt.c violations. Closing it means leaving each bond pad orthogonally for 7 um before turning, which also closes the 3 remaining TM2.b."
    }
  },
